{B.1 = 1-9}
1.	@wDN{Iškur}, the net of the foreign lands …… made the foreign countries praise him duly, 
2.	and made the mighty …… manifest. @wRN{@wDN{Samsu}-iluna}, 
3.	the good hero, lordly one of his Land, 
4.	has wisely co-ordinated decisions for the Land. From the banks of the @wWN{Tigris} and the banks of the @wWN{Euphrates}, 
5.	to the shores of the sea …… and the banks of its rivers, men …… @wRN{@wDN{Samsu}-iluna}. 
6.	In @wTN{E-kur}, the house of @wDN{Enlil}, 
7.	…… he has taken his seat on his dais of joy. @wDN{Enlil}, 
8.	it is sweet to praise you. @wDN{Enlil}, 
9.	give my king a brilliant destiny and years of life! Grant him as a gift a life of long days! 
